<pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I19d8f8d31c1f05dc9d1312daa50be088bf13585e" commit="fd8351d07e9fece2c1295bd2b007256b1091aecd" commit_message="FROMLIST: ath10k: Enable debugfs provision to enable Peer Stats feature  Provide a debugfs entry to enable/ disable Peer Stats feature. Peer Stats feature is for developers/users who are more interested in studying in Rx/Tx stats with multiple clients connected, hence disable this by default. Enabling this feature by default results in unneccessary processing of Peer Stats event for every 500ms and updating peer_stats list (allocating memory) and cleaning it up ifexceeds the higher limit and this can be an unnecessary overhead during long run stress testing.  (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/8599721)  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49260 TEST=built ath10k modules for x86  Change-Id: I19d8f8d31c1f05dc9d1312daa50be088bf13585e Signed-off-by: Mohammed Shafi Shajakhan &lt;mohammed@qti.qualcomm.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Maharaja Kennadyrajan &lt;mkenna@codeaurora.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/333654 Commit-Ready: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="333654" owner_email="c_mkenna@qti.qualcomm.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="9" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/54/333654/9" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ie19e2b0d2a216be3f8e62d369d96771054efece1" commit="20842870154e370591d06b68056816af047b1fa0" commit_message="FROMLIST: ath10k: Introduce Extended Resource Config support for 10.4  Add API support for Extended Resource Configuration for 10.4. This is useful to enable new features like Peer Stats, LTEU etc if the firmware advertises support for the service. This is also done to provide backward compatibility with older firmware. Also for clarity send default host platform type as 'WMI_HOST_PLATFORM_HIGH_PERF', though this should not make any difference in functionality  (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/8599731)  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49260 TEST=built ath10k modules for x86  Change-Id: Ie19e2b0d2a216be3f8e62d369d96771054efece1 Signed-off-by: Mohammed Shafi Shajakhan &lt;mohammed@qti.qualcomm.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Raja Mani &lt;rmani@qti.qualcomm.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Maharaja Kennadyrajan &lt;mkenna@codeaurora.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/333655 Commit-Ready: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Grant Grundler &lt;grundler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="333655" owner_email="c_mkenna@qti.qualcomm.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="9" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/55/333655/9" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I2b41904f3de8f1eab98ab22963355703b0df2080" commit="6855eebd72a49548fe5f4fc09da56b5a24085502" commit_message="FROMLIST: ath10k: Enable parsing per station rx duration for 10.4  Rx duration support for per station is part of extended peer stats, enable provision to parse the same and provide backward compatibility based on the 'stats_id' event  (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/8599741)  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49260 TEST=built ath10k modules for x86  Change-Id: I2b41904f3de8f1eab98ab22963355703b0df2080 Signed-off-by: Mohammed Shafi Shajakhan &lt;mohammed@qti.qualcomm.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Maharaja Kennadyrajan &lt;mkenna@codeaurora.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/333656 Commit-Ready: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="333656" owner_email="c_mkenna@qti.qualcomm.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="9" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/56/333656/9" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I96b2aa7d861eb90dd3428b3e174595a8dfed1831" commit="570bf1f2f295a6842cce5ddcd3584e5ee814d390" commit_message="CHROMIUM: ath10k: enable qca4019 device probe  Update ath10k_ahb_of_match[] to use &quot;qca&quot; instead of &quot;qcom&quot; to match device tree node.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49260 TEST=built ath10k modules for x86  Change-Id: I96b2aa7d861eb90dd3428b3e174595a8dfed1831 Signed-off-by: Raja Mani &lt;rmani@qti.qualcomm.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Maharaja Kennadyrajan &lt;mkenna@codeaurora.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/333653 Commit-Ready: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Grant Grundler &lt;grundler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="333653" owner_email="c_mkenna@qti.qualcomm.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="9" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/53/333653/9" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ida11d249469b03a5264c0b31b6a99afe6cd8ae53" commit="49fdd738fcdfde24c230f94bb10b4be154a1988b" commit_message="FROMLIST: mac80211: introduce netdev queue control for txqs  Until now all stations (notably in AP mode) would share 4 AC queues exposed via netdev. This meant that whenever a single station's AC became full all other stations' AC were considered full and stopped as well.  This was suboptimal and could lead to per station traffic starvation and/or suboptimal Tx aggregation performance.  The introduced queue control is performed by mac80211 alone. Additional netdev queues are created only if driver supports wake_tx_queue() op.  First 4 netdev queues are used for unclassified traffic (e.g. when there's no sta_info for given RA) which is mostly multicast.  All other netdev queues (&gt;=4) are used per station. Each station gets 4 queues for each AC. Whenever station's AC-related ieee80211_txqs get full only that single station's netdev queue is stopped allowing all other stations (either using identical AC number or not) to continue submitting traffic without interruption.  Current implementation supports up to 63 non-overlapping stations. Overlapping stations will share their per AC netdev queues so whenever any of overlapping stations' AC queue is stopped others are stopped as well.  This was designed with MU-MIMO in mind but should benefit regular Tx aggregation as well because drivers will now have the ability to avoid clogging up their internal (be it firmware or hardware) queues with traffic to slow or unresponsive stations needlessly.  Note: This can significantly increase memory usage with, e.g. fq_codel qdisc even up to 20MB per virtual interface.  (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/8134541)  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49260 TEST=built ath10k modules for x86  Change-Id: Ida11d249469b03a5264c0b31b6a99afe6cd8ae53 Signed-off-by: Michal Kazior &lt;michal.kazior@tieto.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Maharaja Kennadyrajan &lt;mkenna@codeaurora.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/334111 Commit-Ready: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="334111" owner_email="c_mkenna@qti.qualcomm.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/11/334111/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I590ae74e7075d9ef755b9eaefcb50de8a552634f" commit="e2dfddb742bf3ec794857f154558a37716d05f87" commit_message="CHROMIUM: mac80211: Fix OOM with newly added more number of netdev queues  After the addition of 256 netdev sub-queues, the memory consumed by every VAP is increased to ~20MB. This buffer bloat causes OOM in testing involves 32-VAPs. Reduce the number of stations exposed for ndev queues from 63 to 16. MU-MIMO gain may need to be analyzed with this change.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49260 TEST=built ath10k modules for x86  Change-Id: I590ae74e7075d9ef755b9eaefcb50de8a552634f Signed-off-by: Vasanthakumar Thiagarajan &lt;vthiagar@qti.qualcomm.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Maharaja Kennadyrajan &lt;mkenna@codeaurora.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/334112 Commit-Ready: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Grant Grundler &lt;grundler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="334112" owner_email="c_mkenna@qti.qualcomm.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/12/334112/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I342311756085eedf94fcee366b236ea24c6c371f" commit="58622c873ec891fb053eb737aa0c7fa56c5778fe" commit_message="CHROMIUM: ath10k: generalizing the firmware code init functions prototype  This patch generalizing the firmware code init functions prototype, to support NORMAL and UTF firmware by adding firmware type in the argument. The UTF support has added in the following patch.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49260 TEST=built ath10k modules for x86  Change-Id: I342311756085eedf94fcee366b236ea24c6c371f Signed-off-by: Tamizh Chelvam &lt;c_traja@qti.qualcomm.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Maharaja Kennadyrajan &lt;mkenna@codeaurora.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/334113 Commit-Ready: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="334113" owner_email="c_mkenna@qti.qualcomm.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/13/334113/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I17fb9a532148d5f61e388c284c6b2c7fa5f81592" commit="c2301688a19e18b5de67497175013ccc55b4775b" commit_message="CHROMIUM: ath10k: Add wmi changes for testmode support  This patch adds wmi changes in 10.2 and 10.4 for testmode support. The changes are common for both 10.2 and 10.4.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49260 TEST=built ath10k modules for x86  Change-Id: I17fb9a532148d5f61e388c284c6b2c7fa5f81592 Signed-off-by: Tamizh Chelvam &lt;c_traja@qti.qualcomm.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Maharaja Kennadyrajan &lt;mkenna@codeaurora.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/334114 Commit-Ready: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Grant Grundler &lt;grundler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="334114" owner_email="c_mkenna@qti.qualcomm.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/14/334114/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="If835de08cbd46fed1a4a21c627088461903a444a" commit="a0d761f5ee74ef98776d18d1614e19a30f95076e" commit_message="CHROMIUM: ath10k: add testmode support for 10.4 firmware  This patch adds testmode support for QCA40XX chipsets which uses 10.4 firmware and added code swap support for UTF binary.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49260 TEST=built ath10k modules for x86  Change-Id: If835de08cbd46fed1a4a21c627088461903a444a Signed-off-by: Tamizh Chelvam &lt;c_traja@qti.qualcomm.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Maharaja Kennadyrajan &lt;mkenna@codeaurora.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/334115 Commit-Ready: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Grant Grundler &lt;grundler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="334115" owner_email="c_mkenna@qti.qualcomm.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/15/334115/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I863cade2732971dc9a8e1818e4e3bd8dc1f0ddb7" commit="08ef57e9aa42a27d44fff3ba6899d5107318c60d" commit_message="HACK: [media] vb2: Don't unmap a dmabuf while dequeueing  The hardware still needs to read from those buffers as reference frames while decoding. To solve the issue, a dmabuf cannot be unmapped when it was dequeued. No memory will leaked since the dmabuf will still be unmapped and detached when the buffer is put.  BUG=None TEST=Play YT and ApiDemo on ARC Signed-off-by: Pawel Osciak &lt;posciak@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: I863cade2732971dc9a8e1818e4e3bd8dc1f0ddb7 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/334103 Commit-Ready: Owen Lin &lt;owenlin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Owen Lin &lt;owenlin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Tomasz Figa &lt;tfiga@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="334103" owner_email="owenlin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/03/334103/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="8155.0.0-rc1"/></manifest>